      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For a master service agreement, you must secure terms that guard against supply chain shocks, like a well-defined *force majeure* clause that outlines what happens when an unexpected event stops supply. You should also negotiate clear pricing mechanisms, perhaps incorporating a capped escalation clause or a review period tied to market indices, to mitigate sudden price spikes. Don't forget to mandate minimum order quantities (MOQs) and clear lead time commitments from the supplier. These clauses help ensure consistent material flow and predictable costs.",
