      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To guard against sneaky behavior, you need ironclad clauses regarding transparency and compliance. A robust *audit right* clause is crucial; this allows your team to inspect their processes and records to ensure they aren't hiding costs or manipulating schedules. You should also insist on a clear *representation and warranty* section, where the supplier formally guarantees the accuracy of all their quotes and delivery timelines. This forces them to stand behind their promises, making it much harder for them to pull a fast one later.",
