    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "audit rights sound good. i'm just worried about the more \"unpredictable\" side of things though. sometimes it feels like these suppliers act like they have a mind of their own, or like there's some hidden chaos they're counting on to get out of their obligations. how do we handle those almost \"unseen\" risks or sudden, irrational changes in their behavior?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Unseen risks and irrational behavior are best managed with strong performance metrics and dispute resolution mechanisms. You need a clear *Service Level Agreement (SLA)* that defines acceptable performance thresholds—if they consistently miss deadlines or quality standards, there must be pre-agreed penalties. Furthermore, insist on a tiered dispute resolution process, starting with mandatory, good-faith negotiation before escalating to mediation or arbitration. This prevents them from unilaterally deciding that a minor issue warrants a complete breakdown of the agreement.",
      "source": "target",
